  "decision": "The paired neighbourhood mixing difference is unresolved; both geographic and climatic nearest-quarter graphs have less opposite-label mixing than their same-species-month composition reference. On the identical 1,626 taxa, simultaneous within-month distance rank slopes are positive on average for geography and climate, but their difference is unresolved. The conditional climate rank coefficient is not positive in a majority of species. Do not claim equal geographic and climatic niches, distinct selection mechanisms, universal local adaptation, or a biological morph-fitness response. This observational result tests a different estimand from the 774-species environmental organization regression."
